{%- comment -%}
  Kofii Flow — Buy together
  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  A fixed set of products presented as one purchase, added to the cart in a
  single request. The conversion lever is average order value: the shopper sees
  the pieces together and buys them in one action instead of three.

  FIXED, NOT A PICK-AND-MIX. Every item is always included; only the variant
  of each is the shopper's to choose.

  THE ONE PLACE THE THEME FORMATS MONEY IN JAVASCRIPT. Everywhere else — the
  cart above all — a figure the browser worked out is forbidden, because it
  eventually disagrees with checkout. The exception is made here, narrowly,
  because the alternative was worse: a bundle whose total sat still while the
  shopper changed a size reads as broken.

  What makes it safe to bound:
    - The first paint is Liquid's. The server renders the total with the same
      `money` filter as every other price, so the figure is exact before any
      script runs and stays exact if none ever does.
    - The format is the shop's own. `money_format` (or `money_with_currency_format`
      when the theme's currency-code setting is on) is handed to the browser as
      a string; the amount is substituted into it. No format is invented.
    - The arithmetic is integer cents, summed from prices Liquid rendered, so
      market pricing and per-variant pricing are already applied.
    - Nothing downstream reads it. It is display only: the cart is still asked
      to state the real total, and the add request sends variant ids alone.

  NO PRODUCT THEME BLOCKS. Blocks in /blocks read `closest.product`, which
  resolves from the template's product — these come from settings, so there is
  no product context for a block to find. The shared snippets are rendered
  directly, as quick-add and the product spotlight both do.

  The add button is `hidden` until <kf-bundle> reveals it: Shopify documents
  the multi-item `items` array for the JSON body only, so there is no reliable
  no-JavaScript path for adding several variants at once. Without the script
  the section is still a usable curated grid — every item shows its price and
  links to its product page.
{%- endcomment -%}

{{ 'section-bundle.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}
<script src="{{ 'kf-cart.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>
<script src="{{ 'kf-bundle.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>

{%- liquid
  assign s = section.settings

  assign items = section.blocks | where: 'type', 'item'

  comment
    The opening total is accumulated here, on the server, from the variant each
    item will actually show as selected — so the first paint matches the
    dropdowns exactly and needs no correction from the browser.
  endcomment
  assign bundle_total = 0
  assign compare_total = 0
  assign available_count = 0

  for block in items
    assign item_product = block.settings.product
    if item_product == blank
      continue
    endif

    unless item_product.available
      continue
    endunless

    assign opening_variant = item_product.selected_or_first_available_variant

    assign available_count = available_count | plus: 1
    assign bundle_total = bundle_total | plus: opening_variant.price

    if opening_variant.compare_at_price > opening_variant.price
      assign compare_total = compare_total | plus: opening_variant.compare_at_price
    else
      assign compare_total = compare_total | plus: opening_variant.price
    endif
  endfor

  assign savings = compare_total | minus: bundle_total

  comment
    The saving is rendered whenever the opening selection has one, and the
    browser keeps it in step from there. Its markup is always present so there
    is an element to fill when a later selection introduces a saving the
    opening one did not have.
  endcomment
  assign show_savings = false
  if savings > 0
    assign show_savings = true
  endif

  assign total_label = 'bundle.total' | t

  assign add_label = 'bundle.add' | t
  assign added_label = 'bundle.added' | t
  assign sold_out_label = 'bundle.sold_out' | t
  assign unavailable_note = 'bundle.unavailable_note' | t
  assign nothing_available = 'bundle.nothing_available' | t

  assign root_class = 'kf-bundle kf-bundle--' | append: s.layout

  assign columns = items.size
  if columns < 1
    assign columns = 1
  endif
  assign root_style = '--kf-bundle-cols: ' | append: columns | append: ';'

  assign media_sizes = '(min-width: 990px) 20vw, 40vw'

  comment
    The same choice kf-price makes, so the running total is formatted exactly
    like every price beside it. The filter used for the OPENING figure and the
    format handed to the browser have to come from one decision — pick them
    apart and the total changes shape the first time a variant is chosen.

    `strip_html` because a money format may legitimately contain markup (some
    shops wrap the amount in a span). Liquid renders that as HTML; the browser
    writes it with textContent, which would print the tags. Stripping it here
    keeps the running figure plain text in that case rather than broken.
  endcomment
  assign money_filter = 'money'
  assign money_format = shop.money_format | strip_html
  if settings.currency_code_enabled
    assign money_filter = 'money_with_currency'
    assign money_format = shop.money_with_currency_format | strip_html
  endif

  comment
    Rendered once here so the markup below picks a ready-made string instead of
    branching on the filter three separate times.
  endcomment
  if money_filter == 'money_with_currency'
    assign bundle_total_money = bundle_total | money_with_currency
    assign compare_total_money = compare_total | money_with_currency
    assign savings_money = savings | money_with_currency
  else
    assign bundle_total_money = bundle_total | money
    assign compare_total_money = compare_total | money
    assign savings_money = savings | money
  endif

  comment
    True when at least one item is present but sold out, which is what decides
    whether the note explaining the omission is worth showing.
  endcomment
  assign has_unavailable = false
-%}

<div {% render 'kf-section-attrs', s: section.settings, extra_class: root_class, style: root_style %}>
  <div class="kf-container">
    {%- if s.heading != blank or s.text != blank -%}
      <header
        class="kf-bundle__header"
        {% render 'kf-motion-attrs',
          animation: s.animation,
          duration: s.animation_duration,
          easing: s.animation_easing,
          trigger: s.animation_trigger %}
      >
        {%- if s.heading != blank -%}
          <h2 class="kf-bundle__heading {{ s.heading_size }}">{{ s.heading | escape }}</h2>
        {%- endif -%}
        {%- if s.text != blank -%}
          <div class="kf-rte kf-text-muted kf-bundle__text">{{ s.text }}</div>
        {%- endif -%}
      </header>
    {%- endif -%}

    <kf-bundle
      class="kf-bundle__inner"
      data-added-label="{{ added_label | escape }}"
      data-money-format="{{ money_format | escape }}"
    >
      <ul
        class="kf-bundle__items"
        role="list"
        {% render 'kf-motion-attrs',
          stagger: s.animation_stagger,
          stagger_delay: s.animation_stagger_delay,
          trigger: s.animation_trigger %}
      >
        {%- for block in items -%}
          {%- liquid
            assign item_product = block.settings.product
            assign item_variant = item_product.selected_or_first_available_variant

            assign item_class = 'kf-bundle__item'
            unless item_product.available
              assign item_class = item_class | append: ' kf-bundle__item--unavailable'
              assign has_unavailable = true
            endunless

            assign variant_label = 'bundle.variant_label' | t: product: item_product.title
          -%}

          <li
            class="{{ item_class }}"
            data-kf-bundle-item
            {% unless item_product.available %}data-kf-bundle-unavailable{% endunless %}
            {% if item_variant %}
              data-variant-id="{{ item_variant.id }}"
              data-price="{{ item_variant.price }}"
              data-compare="{{ item_variant.compare_at_price | default: item_variant.price }}"
            {% endif %}
            {% render 'kf-motion-attrs',
              animation: s.animation,
              duration: s.animation_duration,
              easing: s.animation_easing %}
            {{ block.shopify_attributes }}
          >
            <a class="kf-bundle__media" href="{{ item_product.url }}" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true">
              {%- render 'kf-media',
                image: item_product.featured_media.preview_image,
                ratio: s.media_ratio,
                sizes: media_sizes,
                placeholder: 'product-1'
              -%}
            </a>

            <div class="kf-bundle__info">
              {%- if block.settings.label != blank -%}
                <p class="kf-label kf-text-muted kf-bundle__eyebrow">{{ block.settings.label | escape }}</p>
              {%- endif -%}

              <h3 class="kf-bundle__title kf-text-sm">
                {%- if item_product != blank -%}
                  <a class="kf-bundle__title-link" href="{{ item_product.url }}">{{ item_product.title | escape }}</a>
                {%- else -%}
                  {{ 'products.product.placeholder_title' | t }}
                {%- endif -%}
              </h3>

              {%- if item_product.available -%}
                {%- comment -%}
                  Each variant's price is a full `kf-price` render, hidden until
                  its variant is chosen. Going through the shared snippet is the
                  point: it is what brings the compare-at strikethrough, the
                  on-sale colour, the currency-code setting and unit pricing.

                  This used to emit a bare span holding `{{ v.price | money }}`,
                  which meant a variant on sale rendered as an ordinary price —
                  no "was" figure, no sale styling — while the single-variant
                  branch beside it, which did call kf-price, showed both. One
                  price implementation, or the two drift exactly like that.

                  Gated on the price OR the compare-at varying. Gating on price
                  alone missed the common sale shape where every variant costs
                  the same and only some are discounted: `price_varies` is false
                  there, so a single static price rendered and never changed.
                  Otherwise a 50-variant product would emit 50 identical prices.
                {%- endcomment -%}
                {%- liquid
                  assign per_variant_price = false
                  if item_product.price_varies or item_product.compare_at_price_varies
                    assign per_variant_price = true
                  endif
                -%}
                <div class="kf-bundle__price">
                  {%- if per_variant_price -%}
                    {%- for v in item_product.variants -%}
                      <span
                        data-kf-bundle-price
                        data-variant="{{ v.id }}"
                        {% unless v.id == item_variant.id %}hidden{% endunless %}
                      >
                        {%- render 'kf-price', product: item_product, variant: v, show_from: false -%}
                      </span>
                    {%- endfor -%}
                  {%- else -%}
                    {%- render 'kf-price', product: item_product, variant: item_variant, show_from: false -%}
                  {%- endif -%}
                </div>

                {%- unless item_product.has_only_default_variant -%}
                  <select
                    class="kf-select kf-bundle__variant"
                    data-kf-bundle-variant
                    aria-label="{{ variant_label | escape }}"
                  >
                    {%- for v in item_product.variants -%}
                      <option
                        value="{{ v.id }}"
                        data-price="{{ v.price }}"
                        data-compare="{{ v.compare_at_price | default: v.price }}"
                        {% if v.id == item_variant.id %}selected{% endif %}
                        {% unless v.available %}disabled{% endunless %}
                      >
                        {{ v.title }}{% unless v.available %} — {{ sold_out_label }}{% endunless %}
                      </option>
                    {%- endfor -%}
                  </select>
                {%- endunless -%}
              {%- else -%}
                <p class="kf-badge kf-bundle__sold-out">{{ sold_out_label }}</p>
              {%- endif -%}
            </div>
          </li>
        {%- else -%}
          {%- comment -%}
            Nothing chosen yet. Placeholders keep the section looking
            intentional in the Theme Editor before configuration.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          {%- for i in (1..3) -%}
            <li class="kf-bundle__item kf-bundle__item--placeholder">
              <div class="kf-bundle__media">
                {%- render 'kf-media', ratio: s.media_ratio, placeholder: 'product-1' -%}
              </div>
              <div class="kf-bundle__info">
                <h3 class="kf-bundle__title kf-text-sm">{{ 'products.product.placeholder_title' | t }}</h3>
                <div class="kf-bundle__price">
                  <span class="kf-price__regular kf-text-muted">{{ 1999 | money }}</span>
                </div>
              </div>
            </li>
          {%- endfor -%}
        {%- endfor -%}
      </ul>

      <div class="kf-bundle__summary">
        {%- if available_count > 0 -%}
          <div class="kf-bundle__totals">
            <span class="kf-text-sm kf-text-muted">{{ total_label }}</span>
            <span class="kf-bundle__total">
              <s
                class="kf-text-muted kf-bundle__was"
                data-kf-bundle-was
                {% unless show_savings %}hidden{% endunless %}
              >{{ compare_total_money }}</s>
              <span class="kf-bundle__now" data-kf-bundle-total>{{ bundle_total_money }}</span>
            </span>
            {%- assign savings_label = 'bundle.save' | t: amount: savings_money -%}
            <span
              class="kf-badge kf-badge--accent kf-bundle__savings"
              data-kf-bundle-savings
              data-label="{{ 'bundle.save' | t: amount: '[amount]' | escape }}"
              {% unless show_savings %}hidden{% endunless %}
            >{{ savings_label }}</span>
          </div>

          {%- comment -%}
            Rendered `hidden` and revealed by <kf-bundle>. See the note at the
            top: a multi-item add has no dependable path without the script,
            and a dead button is worse than none.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          <button
            class="kf-button kf-button--lg kf-bundle__add"
            type="button"
            data-kf-bundle-add
            hidden
          >
            <span class="kf-button__label">{{ add_label }}</span>
          </button>

          {%- if has_unavailable -%}
            <p class="kf-text-xs kf-text-muted">{{ unavailable_note }}</p>
          {%- endif -%}
        {%- elsif items.size > 0 -%}
          <p class="kf-text-sm kf-text-muted">{{ nothing_available }}</p>
        {%- endif -%}

        <p class="kf-form-message kf-form-message--error" data-kf-bundle-error role="alert" hidden></p>

        <p class="kf-form-status" data-kf-bundle-status hidden>
          {%- render 'kf-icon', name: 'check', size: 'sm' -%}
          <span>{{ added_label }}</span>
          <a class="kf-link" href="{{ routes.cart_url }}">{{ 'products.product.view_cart' | t }}</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </kf-bundle>
  </div>
</div>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "t:sections.kf-bundle.name",
  "tag": "section",
  "class": "kf-bundle-section",
  "max_blocks": 5,
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "t:sections.kf-bundle.settings.header__1.content"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "heading",
      "label": "t:sections.kf-bundle.settings.heading.label",
      "default": "Buy it together"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "heading_size",
      "label": "t:sections.kf-bundle.settings.heading_size.label",
      "options": [
        {
          "value": "kf-h4",
          "label": "t:sections.kf-bundle.settings.heading_size.options__1.label"
        },
        {
          "value": "kf-h3",
          "label": "t:sections.kf-bundle.settings.heading_size.options__2.label"
        },
        {
          "value": "kf-h2",
          "label": "t:sections.kf-bundle.settings.heading_size.options__3.label"
        }
      ],
      "default": "kf-h3"
    },
    {
      "type": "richtext",
      "id": "text",
      "label": "t:sections.kf-bundle.settings.text.label"
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "t:sections.kf-bundle.settings.header__2.content"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "layout",
      "label": "t:sections.kf-bundle.settings.layout.label",
      "options": [
        {
          "value": "row",
          "label": "t:sections.kf-bundle.settings.layout.options__1.label"
        },
        {
          "value": "stacked",
          "label": "t:sections.kf-bundle.settings.layout.options__2.label"
        }
      ],
      "default": "row"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "media_ratio",
      "label": "t:sections.kf-bundle.settings.media_ratio.label",
      "options": [
        {
          "value": "square",
          "label": "t:sections.kf-bundle.settings.media_ratio.options__1.label"
        },
        {
          "value": "portrait",
          "label": "t:sections.kf-bundle.settings.media_ratio.options__2.label"
        },
        {
          "value": "landscape",
          "label": "t:sections.kf-bundle.settings.media_ratio.options__3.label"
        }
      ],
      "default": "square"
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "t:sections.kf-bundle.settings.header__3.content"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "animation",
      "label": "t:sections.kf-bundle.settings.animation.label",
      "options": [
        {
          "value": "none",
          "label": "t:sections.kf-bundle.settings.animation.options__1.label"
        },
        {
          "value": "fade",
          "label": "t:sections.kf-bundle.settings.animation.options__2.label"
        },
        {
          "value": "fade-up",
          "label": "t:sections.kf-bundle.settings.animation.options__3.label"
        },
        {
          "value": "scale-up",
          "label": "t:sections.kf-bundle.settings.animation.options__4.label"
        }
      ],
      "default": "fade-up"
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "animation_stagger",
      "label": "t:sections.kf-bundle.settings.animation_stagger.label",
      "default": true
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "animation_stagger_delay",
      "label": "t:sections.kf-bundle.settings.animation_stagger_delay.label",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 300,
      "step": 10,
      "unit": "ms",
      "default": 80
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "animation_duration",
      "label": "t:sections.kf-bundle.settings.animation_duration.label",
      "options": [
        {
          "value": "theme",
          "label": "t:sections.kf-bundle.settings.animation_duration.options__1.label"
        },
        {
          "value": "fast",
          "label": "t:sections.kf-bundle.settings.animation_duration.options__2.label"
        },
        {
          "value": "normal",
          "label": "t:sections.kf-bundle.settings.animation_duration.options__3.label"
        },
        {
          "value": "slow",
          "label": "t:sections.kf-bundle.settings.animation_duration.options__4.label"
        }
      ],
      "default": "theme"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "animation_easing",
      "label": "t:sections.kf-bundle.settings.animation_easing.label",
      "options": [
        {
          "value": "theme",
          "label": "t:sections.kf-bundle.settings.animation_easing.options__1.label"
        },
        {
          "value": "standard",
          "label": "t:sections.kf-bundle.settings.animation_easing.options__2.label"
        },
        {
          "value": "smooth",
          "label": "t:sections.kf-bundle.settings.animation_easing.options__3.label"
        },
        {
          "value": "out",
          "label": "t:sections.kf-bundle.settings.animation_easing.options__4.label"
        },
        {
          "value": "spring",
          "label": "t:sections.kf-bundle.settings.animation_easing.options__5.label"
        }
      ],
      "default": "theme"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "animation_trigger",
      "label": "t:sections.kf-bundle.settings.animation_trigger.label",
      "options": [
        {
          "value": "scroll",
          "label": "t:sections.kf-bundle.settings.animation_trigger.options__1.label"
        },
        {
          "value": "load",
          "label": "t:sections.kf-bundle.settings.animation_trigger.options__2.label"
        }
      ],
      "default": "scroll"
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "t:sections.kf-bundle.settings.header__4.content"
    },
    {
      "type": "color_scheme",
      "id": "color_scheme",
      "label": "t:sections.kf-bundle.settings.color_scheme.label",
      "default": "scheme-1"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "section_transition",
      "label": "t:sections.kf-bundle.settings.section_transition.label",
      "options": [
        {
          "value": "none",
          "label": "t:sections.kf-bundle.settings.section_transition.options__1.label"
        },
        {
          "value": "round",
          "label": "t:sections.kf-bundle.settings.section_transition.options__2.label"
        },
        {
          "value": "overlap",
          "label": "t:sections.kf-bundle.settings.section_transition.options__3.label"
        }
      ],
      "default": "none"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "padding_top",
      "label": "t:sections.kf-bundle.settings.padding_top.label",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 200,
      "step": 4,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 64
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "padding_bottom",
      "label": "t:sections.kf-bundle.settings.padding_bottom.label",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 200,
      "step": 4,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 64
    }
  ],
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "item",
      "name": "t:sections.kf-bundle.blocks.item.name",
      "settings": [
        {
          "type": "product",
          "id": "product",
          "label": "t:sections.kf-bundle.blocks.item.settings.product.label"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "label",
          "label": "t:sections.kf-bundle.blocks.item.settings.label.label",
          "info": "t:sections.kf-bundle.blocks.item.settings.label.info"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "presets": [
    {
      "name": "t:sections.kf-bundle.presets.name",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "item"
        },
        {
          "type": "item"
        },
        {
          "type": "item"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
